# Refreshed for each Zenodo deposit in the commit that is tagged, before publication (ADR-0010
# Amendments): the version DOI reserved in the Zenodo draft is added under identifiers (none is
# replaced); version, date-released (the planned publication date) and title become that
# deposit's; doi, the concept DOI, stays. No commit field: the file cannot hold the hash of the
# commit that contains it. version names the tag; the README and the Zenodo record give the hash.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "To cite SYNDEOM, use the concept DOI, which resolves to the latest deposited version. To cite the Gate S1 design registration itself, use its version DOI, listed under identifiers."
title: "SYNDEOM: Calibration Infrastructure for Mathematical Proof Triage — Design Registration at Gate S1"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zalewski
    given-names: Alexander David
    affiliation: DARQ Labs
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9019-7631"
version: gate-s1-registration
date-released: "2026-10-27"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23682780
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23682781
    description: "Version DOI of the Gate S1 design registration"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Quigles1337/Syndeom"
